      "problem": "If $|B|=2$ then $|P(P(P(B)))|=$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|B|=2.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(B)|={2}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(B))| & ={2}^{|P(B)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(B)))| & ={2}^{|P(P(B))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{16} \\\\  & =65\\,536.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
